# bob (ai, seat 1) is the active
# player with TWO creatures already attacking alice (human, seat 0) directly
# — the `|Attacking` marker, no ":ID" (`GameState.java`'s `handleCombat`
# attacks the defending player when none is given). `activephase` lands on
# Declare ATTACKERS Step, not Declare Blockers itself: `GameState.
# applyGameOnThread` runs this combat block BEFORE its own unconditional
# `checkStateEffects(true)`, so landing straight on Declare Blockers reads a
# scripted creature's characteristics one state-effects pass too early and
# Forge offers it as a blocker ZERO times (see the README's own evidence
# link), the same bug `no-creatures.state`/`one-creature.state` avoid the
# same way).
# The test drives bob's own priority stop at Declare Attackers Step through
# the ordinary main loop, which settles state before Declare Blockers opens.
#
# TWO attackers and TWO blockers, not one of each: the undo-offer and
# lasting-arrow proof need a second attacker/blocker pair on the board so
# blocking one, undoing it, and blocking it again never has to be the ONLY
# assignment in play.
#
# Blockers are Wall of Stone (0/8, Defender — can't attack, irrelevant here),
# never Memnite, on purpose: a 1/1 Memnite blocking a 1/1 Memnite is a
# mutual kill, and the e2e proof of the CONFIRMED map (`CombatBand.blockers`,
# read once Forge has moved past declare-blockers) needs both the attacker
# and the blocker still ON THE BOARD after combat damage is dealt — measured
# against the real jar (claws run 37584358566): with two Memnites, combat
# resolves Declare Blockers → Combat Damage → End of Combat → Main 2 in
# under 100ms once nobody has anything to respond with, and BOTH creatures
# are already dead by the first priority stop in Combat Damage Step, so
# `cardBox` finds neither one and no arrow is possible — not a product bug,
# a scenario that killed the very thing it needed to observe. 0 power never
# kills the 1/1 attacker; 8 toughness survives the 1 damage back.
turn=1
activeplayer=ai
activephase=COMBAT_DECLARE_ATTACKERS
humanlife=20
ailife=20
humanhand=
humanbattlefield=Wall of Stone;Wall of Stone
humanlibrary=Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain
humangraveyard=
aihand=
aibattlefield=Memnite|Attacking;Memnite|Attacking
ailibrary=Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain
aigraveyard=
